---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';

/*
  NOT LEGAL ADVICE. This describes accurately what the site as built actually
  does with data — form fields, third-party delivery and logging, GA4, no
  cookies beyond GA4. Have a lawyer review it against PIPEDA and, if EU or UK
  traffic is material, the GDPR before launch. If GA4 is not enabled, delete
  the analytics section.

  Suppliers are described by what they do, not by name, at the client's
  request. That is a deliberate choice with a trade-off attached: naming
  processors is the stronger transparency position under PIPEDA and the GDPR,
  and a corporate client's legal team may ask for the list directly. Be ready
  to supply it on request — and keep this section honest about the two facts
  that actually carry legal weight, which are that third parties are involved
  at all and that data leaves Canada.
*/
---

<Legal
  title="Privacy Policy | DEEJAY T-JR."
  description="How DEEJAY T-JR. collects, uses and stores the information you send through the booking form on deejaytjr.com."
  path="/privacy"
  heading="Privacy policy"
  updated="September 2026"
>
  <p>
    This site exists to take booking enquiries. It collects as little as it can, keeps it only as
    long as it is useful, and never sells it.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <p>When you submit the availability form, we receive what you typed into it:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Your name and email address, which are required so we can reply</li>
    <li>The event type, and optionally the date, city, guest count and budget range</li>
    <li>How you heard about her, and anything you write in the message field</li>
    <li>
      The page you submitted from and any campaign parameters in the link you followed, so we know
      which pages generate genuine enquiries
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The form also contains a hidden field that people never see. If it is filled in, we treat the
    submission as automated and discard it.
  </p>

  <h2>What we do with it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Email it to us at {SITE.email} so a person can reply to you</li>
    <li>Record it in a private lead log so enquiries do not get lost</li>
    <li>Send you an automatic acknowledgement confirming we received it</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    That is all. Your details are not added to a mailing list, not used for marketing, and not
    shared with anyone outside our team.
  </p>

  <h2>Who processes it</h2>
  <p>
    We use a small number of third-party providers to deliver your enquiry to us, to keep a record
    of it, and to host this site. They act only on our instructions, they are not permitted to use
    your information for their own purposes, and some of them store data on servers outside Canada.
    If you would like to know which providers we use, ask us and we will tell you. If you would
    rather not use the form at all, email {SITE.email} directly.
  </p>

  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    We use Google Analytics 4 to count page views and to see which pages lead to enquiries. It sets
    cookies in your browser. We also use our host’s cookieless page counter, which sets no cookies
    and records which pages are visited and when an enquiry is sent, not who sent it. If you arrive from one of our campaign links, the site also keeps a
    small first-party cookie for 30 days recording which link brought you here, so an enquiry can
    be credited to the right campaign. It holds no personal information and is never shared. We do not use it for advertising, we do not build profiles of
    individual visitors, and we do not run any advertising or retargeting pixels on this site.
  </p>

  <h2>Embedded players</h2>
  <p>
    The listen page embeds players from Apple Music and Bandcamp, and the video pages embed
    YouTube. None of them load until you scroll to them or press play, and none autoplay. Once
    loaded, each is served by that company and may set its own cookies under its own privacy
    policy — data we neither control nor receive.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    Enquiries are kept for as long as they may lead to a booking or need to be referenced for one,
    and reviewed periodically after that. You can ask us to delete yours at any time.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask what we hold about you, ask us to correct it, or ask us to delete it. Write to
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> and we will action it. If you are in Canada
    and unhappy with how we respond, you can complain to the Office of the Privacy Commissioner of
    Canada.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes, the date at the top of this page changes with it.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about this policy go to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
  </p>
</Legal>
